  "summary": "This study fabricated two binder-free nickel-foam electrodes: regular NH4HF2-etched Ti3C2 MXene and K+-intercalated Ti3C2 (K-MXene). K-MXene was produced by adding KOH after NH4HF2 etching, yielding a larger XRD (002) spacing (12.4 \u00c5 versus 10.8 \u00c5) and a highly opened layered structure. The primary K-MXene electrode delivered the best reported gravimetric capacitance, 690.9 F g\u22121 at 1 A g\u22121 in 1 M KOH, compared with 333.3 F g\u22121 for regular MXene. Electrode thickness, areal mass loading, pore diameter, porosity, and volumetric/areal capacitance were not reported."
